menu "NEON LINK — Ableton Link"

config NEON_LINK_STUB
    bool "Build with Link stub (no Ableton Link networking)"
    default n
    help
        Replaces the Ableton Link session with a free-running internal
        timeline (fixed tempo, no peers). Used as a CI fallback leg and
        for debugging: everything downstream of the timeline snapshot
        behaves identically.

config NEON_LINK_AUDIO
    bool "Link Audio streaming (needs Ableton Link 4.0)"
    depends on !NEON_LINK_STUB && !NEON_SYNC
    default y if NEON_AUDIO
    default n
    help
        Publish the module's mix (and line input) as named Link Audio
        channels, and play a channel published by Live 12.4 or another
        peer. Requires the Ableton Link submodule checked out at tag
        Link-4.0 — ableton::LinkAudio does not exist before that, and the
        build fails with a message telling you so.

        With this off, everything downstream still builds and runs: the
        Link Audio facade is a no-op whose available() is false, and the
        editor says streaming is not in this firmware.

endmenu
